WEBVTT

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:35.000
BISM ALLAH ARRAHMAN ARRAHIM My dear lucky viewers, Al-Salaamu ‘Alaykum

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:42.000
This tape will present to you how to observe the Contact Prayer, the Salat.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:49.000
And you are very lucky because you are trying to learn how to make contact with your creator,

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.000
which is the greatest of all worships.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:56.000
In this tape, I will explain to you the meaning of the word Salat.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:59.000
You already heard me call it contact.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:05.000
The word Salat (‏صلاة) is an Arabic word derived from the root Silah (صلة),

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:11.000
which means connection or contact. So, when you observe the Salat prayers, you make contact

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:12.000
with your creator.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:16.000
It is wrong to translate it as pray.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:23.000
As a Muslim, when you tell somebody “I pray five times a day”, that is the wrong expression,

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:26.000
because other people can tell you “I pray all day.”

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:34.000
The correct expression for the Muslim is “I make contact with my creator five times a

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:35.000
day.”

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:37.000
This is the meaning of Salat.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:44.000
In this program, I will present to you where the Salat commandment comes from.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:50.000
The Contact Prayer is mention in the Quran more than seventy times.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:58.000
And I will show you the crucial verses, like where the times of Contact Prayers are mentioned

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.000
in the Quran.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:06.000
Then, I will go on to explain to you the source of the Contact Prayers.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:12.000
When was the first time that the contact commandment came to us from God? And how did it come to

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:16.000
our generation? I will explain this to you.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:22.000
Then, I will move on to explain why does God want us to establish contact with Him.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:27.000
Why did God command us to observe the Contact Prayers five times a day?

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.000
What is the reason?

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:34.000
Does God need the Contact Prayers, or do we need the Contact Prayers?

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:42.000
After this, I will go on to explain every aspect of the Contact Prayer.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:47.000
I’m gonna start with the call for the Contact Prayer, the Azan (أَذَان).

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:52.000
I will go through the details, even the historical development of it.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:57.000
I will show you how the words are written in English, the English transliteration.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:03.000
Then, I will go on to the preparation for the Contact Prayers, which is called Wuḍū (وضوء‎)

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:05.000
or ablution.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:08.000
And of course, my sources are always the Quran.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:14.000
There's only one source, and it is this book right here, the Quran.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:18.000
God’s message to you, to me and to the whole world.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:21.000
This is God’s final message to the world.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:25.000
And this is our source, the only source.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:41.000
I will show you where the Wuḍū is mentioned in Quran and what the details are.

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:46.000
Then, I will demonstrate for you how to do the Wuḍū.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:52.000
And I will move on from there to demonstrate for you and describe in detail how to do the

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:55.000
five daily Contact Prayers.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:06:03.000
The Morning Contact, the Noon Contact Prayer, the afternoon, the sunset, and the

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.000
night Contact Prayer.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:13.000
I will explain also some of the fine details of... for example, what happens when you miss

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:16.000
part of the Contact Prayer in a group.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:21.000
You're going to the mosque and you see a group of people praying, you come in late, what to do?

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:24.000
And some other fine detail.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:30.000
So, I hope this will cover everything you need to know about the Contact Prayer.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.000
The most important worship in Islam.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:13.000
You heard me say that the Contact Prayers must be observed five times every day.

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:18.000
Okay, where in the Quran do you find these five times?

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:22.000
They are specifically defined in the Quran.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:29.000
For example, in Sura number 11, AYA or verse number 114,

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:32.000
we see three times of Contact Prayers.

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:39.000
This is what the verse says “You shall observe the Contact Prayers at both ends of

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:42.000
the day, and at night.”

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:45.000
So, here you have three prayer.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:51.000
At both ends of the day, this is the Morning Prayer and the Sunset Prayer.

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:59.000
The Morning Prayer is before sunrise and the Sunset Prayer is immediately after sunset.

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:03.000
And of course, the Night prayer is the last prayer of the day.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:09.000
So, here in this verse, we have three prayers. We are commanded to do these three prayers.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:12.000
The Morning, the Sunset and the Night.

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:20.000
Now, the Noon Prayer is mentioned in Sura number 17, verse number 78

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:26.000
where it says “You shall observe the Contact Prayer when the sun begins to

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:31.000
decline from the highest point at noon.”

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:38.000
So, this is a very specific description of the time of the Contact Prayer at noon.

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:44.000
As soon as the sun begins to decline from its highest spot of the day at noon, you observe

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:46.000
the Noon Contact Prayer.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:55.000
This is Sura 17, verse 78. It says exactly the time of the Contact Prayer at noon.

00:08:55.000 --> 00:09:00.000
So, now we see the Morning Prayer, the Noon Prayer,

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:03.000
the Sunset Prayer, and the Night Prayer.

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:07.000
Well, this accounts for 4 of the prayers. Where is the fifth one?

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:13.000
We find the fifth prayer mentioned in Sura number 2, AYA or verse number

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:17.000
238), two three eight, where it says “You shall observe

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:22.000
all the Contact Prayers, especially the middle prayer.”

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:27.000
The middle contact prayer has to be the Afternoon Prayer because we have the Morning

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:31.000
Prayer, the Noon Prayer, the Sunset Prayer, and the Night Prayer.

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:34.000
These two prayers here and two prayers here, so the middle prayer will be

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:36.000
the Afternoon Prayer.

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:41.000
So, there you have it, all 5 Contact Prayers mentioned in the Quran.

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:47.000
By the way, the Morning Prayer and the Night Contact Prayer are mentioned by name

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:52.000
in verse 58 of Sura 24.

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:55.000
Sura 24, the verse is 58.

00:09:55.000 --> 00:010:01.000
It talks about Salat Al-fajr (صلاة الفجر‎). This is the Morning Contact Prayer, and Salat

00:010:01.000 --> 00:010:05.000
Al-isha (صلاة العشاء). This is the Night Contact Prayer.

00:010:05.000 --> 00:010:12.000
So, all five times of the Contact Prayers are decreed in the Quran.

00:012:10.000 --> 00:012:17.000
And now I would like to discuss with you the source, the original source, of the Contact Prayers.

00:012:17.000 --> 00:012:25.000
When you look in the Quran, you will notice that before Abraham, there was no mention of

00:012:25.000 --> 00:012:28.000
the Contact Prayers, the Salat.

00:012:28.000 --> 00:012:34.000
You notice that Noah was telling his people to just believe in God and ask His forgiveness,

00:012:34.000 --> 00:012:38.000
but there is no mention of the Contact Prayers before Abraham.

00:012:38.000 --> 00:012:45.000
So, the original source of the Contact Prayers is the prophet Abraham who is the father,

00:012:45.000 --> 00:012:47.000
the founder of Islam.

00:012:47.000 --> 00:012:53.000
And we see this very clearly in Sura number 22, verse number 78,

00:012:53.000 --> 00:012:57.000
the last verse of Sura number 22.

00:012:57.000 --> 00:013:02.000
We also see it in Sura 21, verse 73

00:013:02.000 --> 00:013:11.000
where we learn that the Contact Prayers were given to Abraham, as the original founder

00:013:11.000 --> 00:013:13.000
of Islam.

00:013:13.000 --> 00:013:18.000
And we see in Sura 16, verse number 123 that the prophet

00:013:18.000 --> 00:013:21.000
Muhammad followed the ways of Abraham.

00:013:21.000 --> 00:013:27.000
And then we see in Sura number 8 verses 33 to 35,

00:013:27.000 --> 00:013:33.000
and in Sura 9, verse 54, we see that the Salat, the Contact Prayers,

00:013:33.000 --> 00:013:36.000
were practiced before the prophet Muhammad.

00:013:36.000 --> 00:013:42.000
So, all these... you know, a lot of people are under the erroneous impression that the

00:013:42.000 --> 00:013:47.000
prophet Muhammad brought these practices, but they came through prophet Abraham, and this

00:013:47.000 --> 00:013:53.000
is why we do not see the details of how many units per prayer and these kind of details,

00:013:53.000 --> 00:013:55.000
we do not find it in the Quran.

00:013:55.000 --> 00:014:00.000
Although the Quran is complete, perfect, and fully detailed.

00:014:00.000 --> 00:014:07.000
So, the reason the details of the Contact Prayers are not in the Quran is because they were

00:014:07.000 --> 00:014:12.000
already in existence when the Quran was revealed.

00:014:12.000 --> 00:014:17.000
I can tell you to go and buy Crest toothpaste, and you will... I don’t

00:014:17.000 --> 00:014:22.000
have to explain to you what Crest toothpaste is because Crest is already in existence,

00:014:22.000 --> 00:014:26.000
all you need to do is go out in the market and buy it.

00:014:26.000 --> 00:014:32.000
And when the Quran came down, the Contact Prayers, the Salat, were already in existence.

00:014:32.000 --> 00:014:38.000
And this is exactly why in one of the very early Suras, Sura number 73

00:014:38.000 --> 00:014:43.000
Al-Muzzammil, we see the commandment to observe the Contact

00:014:43.000 --> 00:014:48.000
Prayers and the Zakat (the Obligatory Charity), because they were already in existence.

00:014:48.000 --> 00:014:55.000
Abraham being the founder of Islam, what did he contribute to the religion?

00:014:55.000 --> 00:014:59.000
He contributed all the practices of the religion.

00:014:59.000 --> 00:015:05.000
The Contact Prayer, The Zakat charity, The fasting of Ramadan. In fact, we see

00:015:05.000 --> 00:015:13.000
that the fasting of Ramadan was slightly modified in the Quran in Sura number 2, verse 187.

00:015:13.000 --> 00:015:18.000
Also, Hajj. Hajj in Sura number 22, we see that

00:015:18.000 --> 00:015:22.000
it is directly decreed through the prophet Abraham.

00:015:22.000 --> 00:015:27.000
So, Abraham contributed all practices in Islam. You must correct that impression.

00:015:27.000 --> 00:015:31.000
The prophet Muhammad contributed the Quran. That’s it.

00:015:31.000 --> 00:015:37.000
But all the practices existed before the prophet Muhammad. They were in existence when the

00:015:37.000 --> 00:015:39.000
Quran came down.

00:015:51.000 --> 00:015:55.000
Now, we get to the question why should we pray?

00:015:55.000 --> 00:016:00.000
Why should we make contact with our creator every day, five times?

00:016:00.000 --> 00:016:03.000
Repeating the same thing, five times a day?

00:016:03.000 --> 00:016:08.000
Well, the answer... the obvious answer first is that we do it because our creator

00:016:08.000 --> 00:016:12.000
commanded us to do so, in the Quran, as I showed you.

00:016:12.000 --> 00:016:20.000
But what is the mechanism? Why does God ask us to contact Him five times a day?

00:016:20.000 --> 00:016:22.000
Does God benefit from it?

00:016:22.000 --> 00:016:24.000
Do we benefit from it?

00:016:24.000 --> 00:016:31.000
And the answer immediately is God does not need our Contact Prayer. We need the Contact Prayer.

00:016:31.000 --> 00:016:39.000
And we fully understand the reason for decreeing the Contact Prayers if we know who we are.

00:016:39.000 --> 00:016:42.000
You see, most people do not even know who they are.

00:016:42.000 --> 00:016:46.000
You ask a person “who are you?” and they look in the mirror.

00:016:46.000 --> 00:016:49.000
They say “this is me.” And you know something? They are wrong.

00:016:49.000 --> 00:016:53.000
This is not me. This is my body.

00:016:53.000 --> 00:016:57.000
And the body is like a garment that we are wearing temporarily.

00:016:57.000 --> 00:017:04.000
The real person is invisible to us. The real person, the soul, is in another dimension

00:017:04.000 --> 00:017:07.000
that is not visible to our eyes.

00:017:07.000 --> 00:017:10.000
So, what does the real person look like?

00:017:10.000 --> 00:017:15.000
This will lead us to understanding why should we observe the Contact Prayer.

00:017:15.000 --> 00:017:23.000
You see, you can consider the Contact Prayers the meals for the real person, the food, the nutrition.

00:017:23.000 --> 00:017:28.000
When we are born our mother feeds us milk and we grow.

00:017:28.000 --> 00:017:34.000
Then, we eat all kinds of food, rice and meat and potatoes and so on, and our body grows

00:017:34.000 --> 00:017:38.000
until it becomes five feet, six feet, whatever.

00:017:38.000 --> 00:017:41.000
And that is the limit of the body’s growth.

00:017:41.000 --> 00:017:45.000
Okay. Meanwhile, what is happening to the real person, the soul?

00:017:45.000 --> 00:017:53.000
The body or the garment grows to five or six feet, but what happens to the real person?

00:017:53.000 --> 00:017:58.000
Is the real person nourished just like the body?

00:017:58.000 --> 00:018:06.000
And this is where most people do not realize the importance of making contact with their creator.

00:018:06.000 --> 00:018:11.000
Making contact with our creator is the most important nutrition for the soul.

00:018:11.000 --> 00:018:18.000
We need it to grow and develop. And I'm talking here about the real person.

00:018:18.000 --> 00:018:24.000
The real person grows and develops by contacting our creator daily.

00:018:24.000 --> 00:018:29.000
Five times every day constitutes five meals for the soul.

00:018:29.000 --> 00:018:34.000
So, every time you do a Contact Prayer, your soul grows and develops.

00:018:34.000 --> 00:018:38.000
And this is why we are commanded to do the Contact Prayer.

00:018:38.000 --> 00:018:45.000
You can imagine the person who does not feed his or her soul. At the end of living in this

00:018:45.000 --> 00:018:50.000
world, they are still babies because they never feed their soul.

00:018:50.000 --> 00:018:56.000
But the Muslim, the person who observes the duties and practices of worship,

00:018:56.000 --> 00:019:01.000
this person feeds the soul, and the soul grows and develops immensely.

00:019:01.000 --> 00:019:08.000
And we end up our mission in this world, grown and developed, and healthy, and fit for the

00:019:08.000 --> 00:019:12.000
real life, the eternal life that comes after this life.

00:019:12.000 --> 00:019:22.000
The Contact Prayers therefore are very important. Think of them as the meal for the soul, for the real person.

00:019:22.000 --> 00:019:28.000
The Morning Prayer is the breakfast for the soul, for you, the real you. Just like how you give

00:019:28.000 --> 00:019:34.000
your body breakfast, lunch and dinner, you need, for yourself, the real person, you

00:019:34.000 --> 00:019:37.000
need meals also.

00:019:37.000 --> 00:019:40.000
The Noon Prayer is lunch for the soul.

00:019:40.000 --> 00:019:42.000
And the Afternoon Prayer is another meal.

00:019:42.000 --> 00:019:47.000
And the Sunset Prayer is an meal, nutrition for the real person.

00:019:47.000 --> 00:019:53.000
And the Night Contact Prayer is the dinner for the soul.

00:019:53.000 --> 00:020:00.000
So, nourishing, developing and growing the soul is the reason for observing the Contact

00:020:00.000 --> 00:020:04.000
Prayers, and we are the ones who need it. God does not need it.

00:020:19.000 --> 00:020:26.000
All practices of worship in Islam, without exception, are designed to cause the soul,

00:020:26.000 --> 00:020:30.000
the real person, the real you, to grow and develop.

00:020:30.000 --> 00:020:35.000
They're all designed to make you the boss over your body.

00:020:35.000 --> 00:020:40.000
A lot of people, in fact the majority of people, are enslaved to their body,

00:020:40.000 --> 00:020:44.000
their outer garment, that is temporary.

00:020:44.000 --> 00:020:52.000
Some day this garment is going to vanish and you, the real person, will remain forever, for eternity.

00:020:52.000 --> 00:020:58.000
So, most people, unfortunately, are unaware of nourishing and strengthening and developing

00:020:58.000 --> 00:021:00.000
their soul, the real person.

00:021:00.000 --> 00:021:08.000
But all practices of worship in Islam are designed to cause the soul to grow and develop,

00:021:08.000 --> 00:021:09.000
nourish the soul.

00:021:09.000 --> 00:021:13.000
For example, the Morning Prayer, let’s take the Morning Contact Prayer.

00:021:13.000 --> 00:021:19.000
Before sunrise, what does the body... what does your body want?

00:021:19.000 --> 00:021:22.000
Your body wants to sleep, right?

00:021:22.000 --> 00:021:30.000
But your soul, you, the real you, the real person, needs to get up, do the ablution,

00:021:30.000 --> 00:021:37.000
and observe the Contact Prayer, make contact, the first contact of the day with your creator.

00:021:37.000 --> 00:021:43.000
So, immediately you can see that there is a fight. The body wants to sleep, and the soul needs

00:021:43.000 --> 00:021:49.000
to get up and nourish itself and have breakfast.

00:021:49.000 --> 00:021:56.000
Now, who's going to win? If your body wins, you continue to sleep.

00:021:56.000 --> 00:022:04.000
And the body is the temporary garment. It is not very smart to let the body win, right?

00:022:04.000 --> 00:022:12.000
If you win, you, the real person, win, your body will obey and will say “yes, sir”

00:022:12.000 --> 00:022:19.000
will listen to you, obey you, get up out of bed, do the ablution, and observe the Contact Prayer.

00:022:19.000 --> 00:022:27.000
So, you can see that the first Contact Prayer is a struggle between you and your body.

00:022:27.000 --> 00:022:33.000
By the way, this struggle becomes less and less, as your body becomes more and more obedient

00:022:33.000 --> 00:022:40.000
to you, as you become the boss. As you develop and become stronger, your body becomes more and more

00:022:40.000 --> 00:022:46.000
obedient, and with time, your body, when you say “my body get up and do the Morning

00:022:46.000 --> 00:022:49.000
Prayer”, your body will say “yes, sir” obediently.

00:022:49.000 --> 00:022:57.000
As a matter of fact, eventually, you will actually enjoy getting up in the morning and doing the Contact Prayer.

00:022:57.000 --> 00:023:04.000
And this is because the soul has grown and developed, and became the boss, and enjoys

00:023:04.000 --> 00:023:07.000
observing the contact with our creator.

00:023:07.000 --> 00:023:13.000
You look at the fasting, for example. One of the important practices in Islam is fasting

00:023:13.000 --> 00:023:16.000
the month of Ramadan, during the month of Ramadan.

00:023:16.000 --> 00:023:27.000
And, in Ramadan, your body, of course, wants to eat and drink, but you tell your body when you fast,

00:023:27.000 --> 00:023:30.000
“you're not gonna eat or drink until sunset.”

00:023:30.000 --> 00:023:37.000
So, you can see that you are practicing, exercising your soul, and this causes your soul to grow

00:023:37.000 --> 00:023:41.000
and develop, and this is exactly the whole idea of our being here in this world.

00:023:41.000 --> 00:023:49.000
We want to grow and develop as much as possible in order to enter the real life, the eternal life

00:023:49.000 --> 00:023:55.000
the Hereafter, in a state of fitness, strength, growth and development.

00:023:55.000 --> 00:024:02.000
Because in the Hereafter, you cannot hold a responsible position in the eternal real

00:024:02.000 --> 00:024:05.000
life if you are weak, unnourished, and still a baby.

00:024:05.000 --> 00:024:10.000
Will you hire a baby as a pilot, or an engineer? Of course not.

00:024:10.000 --> 00:024:16.000
So, God wants you to develop yourself and to be strong enough to hold a responsible position,

00:024:16.000 --> 00:024:21.000
a high rank, in the Hereafter, the eternal real life.

00:024:21.000 --> 00:024:27.000
And all practices of worship in Islam are designed towards this end.

00:024:27.000 --> 00:024:30.000
For example, the Zakat charity, what is it?

00:024:30.000 --> 00:024:36.000
The Zakat charity is simply taking money away from your body and giving it to the poor.

00:024:36.000 --> 00:024:42.000
So, you can see that you are being the boss because the body loves money. And you take something

00:024:42.000 --> 00:024:44.000
the the body loves and give it away.

00:024:44.000 --> 00:024:51.000
So, all practices of worship in Islam are designed to make your soul grow and develop,

00:024:51.000 --> 00:024:54.000
make you the boss over your body.

00:024:54.000 --> 00:024:58.000
And the Contact Prayers are the most important tool to do so.

00:024:58.000 --> 00:025:06.000
You're gonna notice it the first time you do the Morning Contact Prayer before sunrise.

00:025:06.000 --> 00:025:12.000
Let us now get to the details of the Contact Prayers and how to observe them.

00:025:12.000 --> 00:025:18.000
There are a billion Muslims in the world today, 1000 million throughout

00:025:18.000 --> 00:025:21.000
the world, in every country of the world.

00:025:21.000 --> 00:025:27.000
But in the area that is recognized as the Muslim world, you hear the call for the prayer

00:025:27.000 --> 00:025:33.000
