00:046:22.000 --> 00:046:28.000
So, this organizational point dictates on us that we must face the direction of Mecca,

00:046:28.000 --> 00:046:30.000
wherever you might be.

00:046:30.000 --> 00:046:39.000
So, in the United States, the direction generally is slightly south of east, slightly south

00:046:39.000 --> 00:046:42.000
of east, southeast.

00:046:42.000 --> 00:046:48.000
So, find the direction of Mecca. You face that direction and then you make your intention.

00:046:48.000 --> 00:046:50.000
This is the first step.

00:046:50.000 --> 00:046:55.000
You must say “I intend to do the Morning Prayer” in any language you like.

00:046:55.000 --> 00:047:01.000
If you want it in Arabic, you can say “Nawaytu Salat Al-Sobh.” This will be the NIYYA or

00:047:01.000 --> 00:047:03.000
the intention for the Morning Prayer.

00:047:03.000 --> 00:047:11.000
Or if it is for the Noon Prayer, you say, in your heart or in an audible voice “I intend

00:047:11.000 --> 00:047:16.000
to do the Noon Prayer”, “Nawaytu Salat Al-Zuhr” in Arabic.

00:047:16.000 --> 00:047:22.000
If it is the Afternoon Prayer, it is “Nawaytu Salat Al-Asr.”

00:047:22.000 --> 00:047:29.000
And for the Sunset Prayer, the NIYYA or intention is “Nawaytu Salat Al-Maghrib.”

00:047:29.000 --> 00:047:36.000
For the Night Prayer, the intention or the NIYYA is “Nawaytu Salat Al-'Eshaa.”

00:047:36.000 --> 00:047:41.000
So, but you can do it in any language you wish, secretly or loudly.

00:047:41.000 --> 00:047:46.000
Now after you do the NIYYA, now you're facing the direction of Mecca, you make your intention

00:047:46.000 --> 00:047:52.000
or NIYYA, then you open the Salat by raising your hands to the sides of your face and saying

00:047:52.000 --> 00:047:57.000
“Allahu akbar” like this “Allahu akbar.

00:047:57.000 --> 00:048:00.000
There is your opening of the Salat.

00:048:00.000 --> 00:048:11.000
Once you say “Allahu Akbar” in this manner, you have started your contact or Salat, your contact with your creator.

00:048:11.000 --> 00:048:18.000
Now after you make the opening TAKBIR, Allahu akbar, you can either put your hands on the side

00:048:18.000 --> 00:048:22.000
or you can choose to hold them like this, with your left hand

00:048:22.000 --> 00:048:27.000
on your stomach, and your right hand on top of your left hand. It doesn’t

00:048:27.000 --> 00:048:32.000
make any difference. Some people make a big deal out of it, but there is no difference.

00:048:32.000 --> 00:048:33.000
Either way is correct.

00:048:33.000 --> 00:048:37.000
So, this is the opening of the Salat, the Contact Prayer.

00:048:37.000 --> 00:048:41.000
Allahu akbar.

00:048:41.000 --> 00:048:46.000
Now, you are ready to recite Al-Fãtehah, the opening Sura of Quran.

00:048:48.000 --> 00:048:55.000
The easiest way for you is to have me write the words in English transliteration, English letters.

00:048:55.000 --> 00:049:02.000
So, before you do the Wuḍū, the ablution, you can say your intention “I intend to

00:049:02.000 --> 00:049:06.000
make the ablution” or Wuḍū either in English or in Arabic.

00:049:06.000 --> 00:049:12.000
So “I intend to do the ablution” in English, the Arabic would be “Nawaytu Al-Wuḍū”.

00:049:12.000 --> 00:049:28.000
And you write it like this “Nawaytu.” “Nawaytu” which means “I intend.”

00:049:28.000 --> 00:049:32.000
Nawaytu Al-Wuḍū.

00:049:32.000 --> 00:049:35.000
“Al” means “the.”

00:049:35.000 --> 00:049:45.000
Ablution “Wuḍū”, “Al-Wuḍū.”

00:049:45.000 --> 00:049:50.000
“Nawaytu Al-Wuḍū”

00:049:50.000 --> 00:049:58.000
Let me write the words of Azaan for you. “Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar Allahu Akbar,

00:049:58.000 --> 00:050:00.000
La Elaha Ella Allah.”

00:050:00.000 --> 00:050:04.000
So, in the Azaan, we say “Allahu Akbar” 4 times.

00:050:04.000 --> 00:050:17.000
“Allahu Akbar“ meaning “God is the greatest.” Allahu

00:050:17.000 --> 00:050:30.000
“Allahu”, “God” “Akbar” (greatest).

00:050:30.000 --> 00:050:36.000
Allahu Akbar, 4 times.

00:050:36.000 --> 00:050:39.000
Then, “La Elaha Ella Allah.”

00:050:39.000 --> 00:050:41.000
“La” means no.

00:050:44.000 --> 00:050:45.000
La

00:050:45.000 --> 00:050:53.000
“Elaha” meaning god with a small g.

00:051:00.000 --> 00:051:04.000
“La” means no. Elaha is god.

00:051:04.000 --> 00:051:06.000
no

00:051:06.000 --> 00:051:09.000
Elaha is god with a small g.

00:051:12.000 --> 00:051:15.000
“Ella” means except.

00:051:19.000 --> 00:051:23.000
Ella, except

00:051:28.000 --> 00:051:39.000
Allah means God.

00:051:43.000 --> 00:051:45.000
“La Elaha Ella Allah“

00:051:45.000 --> 00:051:53.000
So, this is the complete Azaan, the original Azaan without any innovations or additions

00:051:53.000 --> 00:051:56.000
or traditions.

00:051:56.000 --> 00:052:02.000
A lot of people think that Allah is the name of God, but it is not. Allah simply means God.

00:052:02.000 --> 00:052:05.000
The English word for it is God.

00:052:05.000 --> 00:052:11.000
The non-Muslims in the Arabic world say “Allah” because this is the Arabic word for God

00:052:11.000 --> 00:052:13.000
even though they are not Muslims.

00:052:13.000 --> 00:052:18.000
They will say “IN SHAA ALLAH.” They say “Allah” and because simply that is the language.

00:052:18.000 --> 00:052:25.000
It is not the name of God. This is why I use the word, the English word, “God” for Allah.

00:052:28.000 --> 00:052:34.000
Allahu Akbar Allahu Akbar

00:052:37.000 --> 00:052:44.000
Allahu Akbar Allahu Akbar

00:052:45.000 --> 00:052:50.000
La Elaha Ella Allah

00:052:52.000 --> 00:052:57.000
I'm going to write the NIYYA or intention for every prayer for you, so you can see how

00:052:57.000 --> 00:052:59.000
it is spelled.

00:052:59.000 --> 00:053:04.000
Here's the NIYYA or intention for the Morning Prayer.

00:053:04.000 --> 00:053:16.000
“Nawaytu” – “Nawaytu” which means “I intend.

00:053:16.000 --> 00:053:41.000
“Salat” – “Salat Al-Subh” – “Al” – “Subh” – “Al-Subh”

00:053:41.000 --> 00:053:47.000
“I intend to do the Morning Prayer” – “Nawaytu Salat Al-Subh.”

00:053:47.000 --> 00:053:56.000
Now, to make it the Noon Prayer, you just... you say the same thing except you change

00:053:56.000 --> 00:054:02.000
“Al-Subh” to “Zuhr” which means “noon.”

00:054:02.000 --> 00:054:07.000
“Nawaytu” – “Nawaytu Salat Al-Zuhr.”

00:054:07.000 --> 00:054:16.000
This will make it the Noon Prayer, “Al-Zuhr.”

00:054:16.000 --> 00:054:20.000
For the Afternoon Prayer, you just make it “Al-'Asr”

00:054:20.000 --> 00:054:38.000
“Salat Al-'Asr.” You write 'A like this Al-'Asr. “Nawaytu Salat Al-'Asr.”

00:054:38.000 --> 00:054:45.000
The Sunset, you make it “Al-Maghrib.”

00:054:45.000 --> 00:055:03.000
“Nawaytu Salat Al-Maghrib”, it's written like this “Al-Maghrib.”

00:055:03.000 --> 00:055:08.000
“Nawaytu Salat Al-Maghrib.” This is the Sunset Prayer.

00:055:08.000 --> 00:055:13.000
And the Night Prayer is “Al-'Eshaa.”

00:055:13.000 --> 00:055:27.000
“Nawaytu Salat Al-'Eshaa” – “Al-'Eshaa.”

00:055:27.000 --> 00:055:34.000
“Nawaytu Salat Al-'Eshaa.”

00:055:34.000 --> 00:055:42.000
By now you know how Allahu akbar is written, the opening of the Contact Prayer “Allahu akbar.

00:055:42.000 --> 00:055:45.000
This is followed by Sura Al-Fãtehah.

00:055:45.000 --> 00:056:02.000
And it is written like this: The first verse is “Bism Allah.”

00:056:02.000 --> 00:056:13.000
“Arrahman.”

00:056:13.000 --> 00:056:29.000
“Arraheem.”

00:056:29.000 --> 00:056:34.000
“Bism Allah Arrahman Arraheem.”

00:056:34.000 --> 00:056:46.000
“Al hamdu”

00:056:46.000 --> 00:056:54.000
“Lillahi”

00:056:54.000 --> 00:057:14.000
“Rabbil ‘Alameen”

00:057:14.000 --> 00:057:21.000
Okay, “Bism Allah Arrahman Arraheem” means “in the name of God, most Gracious,

00:057:21.000 --> 00:057:23.000
most Merciful.”

00:057:23.000 --> 00:057:28.000
“Al hamdu Lillahi” means “praise be to God.

00:057:28.000 --> 00:057:34.000
“Rabbil ‘Alameen” means “Lord of the universe.”

00:057:34.000 --> 00:057:41.000
“Bism Allah Arrahman Arraheem. Al hamdu Lillahi Rabbil ‘Alameen”, “in the name

00:057:41.000 --> 00:057:49.000
of God, most Gracious, most Merciful. Praise be to God, Lord of the universe.”

00:057:49.000 --> 00:058:12.000
And the next statement is familiar to you: “Arrahman Arraheem”, “Most Gracious

00:058:12.000 --> 00:058:19.000
Most Merciful.”

00:058:19.000 --> 00:058:33.000
And the next statement is: “Maliki” means “Master” or “King.”

00:058:33.000 --> 00:058:51.000
“Yawm” means day. “Eddeen”; recompense. Yawm Eddeen day of recompense.

00:058:51.000 --> 00:058:57.000
So “Arrahman Arraheem”, “Most Gracious, Most Merciful”, “Maliki Yawm Eddeen”,

00:058:57.000 --> 00:059:00.000
“Master of the Day of Recompense.”

00:059:00.000 --> 00:059:30.000
“Eyyaka Na’abudu” means “only You we worship.”

00:059:30.000 --> 00:059:33.000
“Wa Eyyaka” means “and only You”

00:059:33.000 --> 00:059:36.000
“Wa” means “and.”

00:059:36.000 --> 00:059:59.000
“Eyyaka Nasta’aeen” means “we ask for help, only You we ask for help.”

00:059:59.000 --> 01:00:07.000
“Wa Eyyaka Nasta’aeen”, “and only You we ask for help.”

01:00:07.000 --> 01:00:15.000
The next statement... now, of course, you can always go back, reverse the tape and watch

01:00:15.000 --> 01:00:24.000
all these words until you know them very well by heart.

01:00:24.000 --> 01:00:31.000
The next statement is “Ehdina Al-Serata Al-Mustaqeem”, “guide us in the right path.

01:00:31.000 --> 01:00:40.000
“Ehdina” means “guide us.”

01:00:40.000 --> 01:00:51.000
“Al-Serata” means “the path”.

01:00:51.000 --> 01:01:05.000
“Al-Mustaqeem”, “the straight” or the right path.

01:01:08.000 --> 01:01:14.000
“Ehdina Al-Serata Al-Mustaqeem”, “guide us in the right path.”

01:01:14.000 --> 01:01:26.000
“Serata” means “the path of”

01:01:26.000 --> 01:01:36.000
“Al-Lazeena” means “the path of those”

01:01:36.000 --> 01:01:44.000
“An’amta” means “those whom You blessed.”

01:01:44.000 --> 01:01:55.000
“An’amta ‘Alayhim”, “You showered Your blessings on them.”

01:01:55.000 --> 01:02:00.000
“Ehdina Al-Serata Al-Mustaqeem”, “guide us in the right path.”

01:02:00.000 --> 01:02:09.000
“Serata Al-Lazeena An’amta ‘Alayhim”, “the path of those whom you blessed.”

01:02:09.000 --> 01:02:22.000
And then we go to the last statement in the Al-Fãtehah, “Ghayri Al-Maghdoobi ‘Alayhim.”

01:02:22.000 --> 01:02:31.000
“Ghayri” means “other than, or not.”

01:02:31.000 --> 01:02:54.000
“Al-Maghdoobi ‘Alayhim” means “not the path of those who incur wrath, or anger.”

01:02:54.000 --> 01:02:56.000
“Ghayri Al-Maghdoobi ‘Alayhim.”

01:02:56.000 --> 01:02:58.000
“Wa Laddaalleen” (not the strayers).

01:02:58.000 --> 01:03:00.000
“Wa” means “and.”

01:03:00.000 --> 01:03:03.000
“La” means “no”, “nor” “Wa La”

01:03:03.000 --> 01:03:13.000
“Wa Laddaalleen”, and this is the end of it – “and not the strayers.”

01:03:13.000 --> 01:03:18.000
“Ghayri Al-Maghdoobi ‘Alayhim”, “not the path of those who incur wrath, or anger”

01:03:18.000 --> 01:03:22.000
“Wa Laddaalleen”, “nor the strayers.”

01:03:42.000 --> 01:03:48.000
After you recite Al-Fãtehah, then you make Ruku, bowing.

01:03:48.000 --> 01:03:54.000
And as you bow you say “Allahu Akbar” and you know what that looks like. I wrote it for you.

01:03:54.000 --> 01:04:00.000
Then during the Ruku you say “Subhaana Rabbiya Al-‘Azeem” about three times. It doesn’t

01:04:00.000 --> 01:04:02.000
matter, two or three or four times.

01:04:02.000 --> 01:04:12.000
“Subhaana” means “glory be to.”

01:04:12.000 --> 01:04:22.000
“Subhaana Rabbiya” means “Glory be to my Lord.”

01:04:22.000 --> 01:04:31.000
“Al-‘Azeem” means “the Great.”

01:04:31.000 --> 01:04:38.000
“Subhaana Rabbiya Al-‘Azeem”, “Glory be to my Lord, the Great.”

01:04:38.000 --> 01:04:47.000
Then, you stand up and in this position only you say “Sami’a Allahu Leman Hamidah”

01:04:47.000 --> 01:04:50.000
means “God hears anyone who praises Him.”

01:04:50.000 --> 01:05:09.000
And it is written like this “Sami’a Allahu”

01:05:09.000 --> 01:05:17.000
“Leman”, “anyone.”

01:05:17.000 --> 01:05:25.000
“Hamidah”, “who praises him.”

01:05:25.000 --> 01:05:31.000
“Sami’a Allahu Leman Hamidah” as you stand up.

01:05:31.000 --> 01:05:39.000
Then, you make the first prostration, Sujud.

01:05:39.000 --> 01:05:44.000
And when you do that, you say “Allahu Akbar” as you go down in prostration.

01:05:44.000 --> 01:05:58.000
And during prostration, you say “Subhaana Rabbiya Al-A‘alaa”

01:05:58.000 --> 01:06:05.000
about three or four times, means “Glory be to my lord, the Most High.”

01:06:05.000 --> 01:06:09.000
“Al-A‘alaa”, “the Most High.”

01:06:09.000 --> 01:06:13.000
And this takes care of all the words of the Contact Prayers.

01:06:13.000 --> 01:06:19.000
Now, you know how to say all the words and if you play the tape over and over, you can

01:06:19.000 --> 01:06:23.000
see how exactly they are written down and how they are pronounced.

01:07:17.000 --> 01:07:24.000
In the sitting position, you say “Ash-hadu Alla Elaha Ella Allah, Wahdahu La Shareeka Lah

01:07:24.000 --> 01:07:30.000
which means “I bear witness that there is no god except Allah, the one God,

01:07:30.000 --> 01:07:30.000
He is one.

01:07:30.000 --> 01:07:33.000
“La Shareeka Lah”, “He has no partners.”

01:07:33.000 --> 01:07:43.000
And this is how I write it “Ash-hadu” means “I bear witness.”

01:07:43.000 --> 01:07:49.000
“Ash-hadu Alla”,

01:07:49.000 --> 01:07:53.000
“Elaha” means “god with a small g.”

01:07:53.000 --> 01:07:56.000
“I bear witness that there is no god”

01:07:56.000 --> 01:08:01.000
“Ella”, “except”

01:08:01.000 --> 01:08:08.000
“Ella Allah”, “the one God”

01:08:08.000 --> 01:08:18.000
“Wahdahu”, “He is one”

01:08:18.000 --> 01:08:22.000
“Wahdahu La Shareeka Lah”, “He has no partner.”

01:08:22.000 --> 01:08:25.000
“La” means “no.”

01:08:25.000 --> 01:08:28.000
“Shareek” means “partner.”

01:08:28.000 --> 01:08:38.000
“La Shareeka Lah”, (He has no partner).

01:08:38.000 --> 01:08:44.000
And this takes care of the Ta-shahud in the sitting position,

01:08:44.000 --> 01:08:53.000
“Ash-hadu Alla Elaha Ella Allah, Wahdahu La Shareeka Lah.”

01:08:53.000 --> 01:08:59.000
And then of course to end the prayer, you look at the right side and say “Al-Salaamu ‘Alaykum”,

01:08:59.000 --> 01:09:04.000
and then on the left side saying “Al-Salaamu ‘Alaykum” and this ends the Contact Prayer.

01:09:04.000 --> 01:09:10.000
So, let me write “Al-Salaamu ‘Alaykum” for you.

01:09:10.000 --> 01:09:28.000
“Al-Salaamu ‘Alaykum”

01:09:28.000 --> 01:09:37.000
There you have it, the complete words of the Contact Prayers.

01:09:37.000 --> 01:09:42.000
Now, let me explain a few fine details about the Salat, the Contact Prayers.

01:09:42.000 --> 01:09:50.000
One of the most important points is that there is a myth among the average Muslims

01:09:50.000 --> 01:09:55.000
that a woman who has her period or menstruation cannot pray.

01:09:55.000 --> 01:10:01.000
Now, this has to be from Satan because Satan is the one who does not want you, the Muslim

01:10:01.000 --> 01:10:02.000
woman, to pray.

01:10:02.000 --> 01:10:08.000
God did not say in the Quran at all “do not pray during menstruation.”

01:10:08.000 --> 01:10:10.000
There is nothing in the Quran that says that.

01:10:10.000 --> 01:10:15.000
Even the Hadith... we learn from Hadith that the prophet’s wives used to pray during

01:10:15.000 --> 01:10:17.000
their menstruation.

01:10:17.000 --> 01:10:22.000
One Hadith even says they put a bucket under one of his wives as she prayed.

01:10:22.000 --> 01:10:28.000
Ridiculous as this may be, but it demonstrates that the Muslim woman should pray during her

01:10:28.000 --> 01:10:29.000
menstruation.

01:10:29.000 --> 01:10:36.000
If a Muslim woman does not pray, during menstruation, this means one week in the month without prayer,

01:10:36.000 --> 01:10:42.000
and this is like 4 years every 10 years, 4 years without any

01:10:42.000 --> 01:10:44.000
prayer, imagine that.

01:10:44.000 --> 01:10:50.000
So, this will be a satanic innovation to stop the women from praying during menstruation.

01:10:50.000 --> 01:10:57.000
So, please, menstruation or not, the Contact Prayer, the Salat prayer is the only worship

01:10:57.000 --> 01:11:03.000
that must go on. There is absolutely no excuse for not doing the Contact Prayer.

01:11:03.000 --> 01:11:09.000
Even God provides that you can pray walking, or riding in a car, or riding in a plane,

01:11:09.000 --> 01:11:16.000
or in a bus, or even if a person is very sick, very ill, cannot move, that person can pray

01:11:16.000 --> 01:11:21.000
with his or her eyelids, or even mentally.

01:11:21.000 --> 01:11:26.000
If you are working in crowded place and you cannot find a place to pray, you can pray

01:11:26.000 --> 01:11:31.000
at your desk sitting down just mentally going through the motions and the words.

01:11:31.000 --> 01:11:36.000
So, there is absolutely no excuse for missing any Contact Prayer.

01:11:53.000 --> 01:12:00.000
So, whether the person is ill, unable to move, or riding, trapped in a car or a bus or

01:12:00.000 --> 01:12:07.000
a plane, or in a working place where there is no place available for prayer,

01:12:07.000 --> 01:12:14.000
or during menstruation, or the after birth bleeding, any of these conditions cannot... nothing

01:12:14.000 --> 01:12:19.000
stops your from performing, observing the Contact Prayers.

01:12:19.000 --> 01:12:25.000
Another point that I wish to mention is the group prayer or the Jama’a.

01:12:25.000 --> 01:12:31.000
In the Jama’a, one person leads the prayer and the rest of the group stand behind him,

01:12:31.000 --> 01:12:39.000
behind the imam, and do exactly what he does. You do not have to recite Al-Fãtehah or the Quran

01:12:39.000 --> 01:12:42.000
after the imam.

01:12:42.000 --> 01:12:49.000
Remember, all that is required in the Contact Prayer is the Al-Fãtehah, the first Sura of Quran.

01:12:49.000 --> 01:12:56.000
So, you just mentally follow the imam as he recites Al-Fãtehah during the Contact Prayer.

01:12:56.000 --> 01:13:02.000
And then of course in Ruku', the bowing position, you say “Subhaana Rabbiya Al-‘Azeem” as usual.

01:13:02.000 --> 01:13:09.000
And in the Sujood or prostration, you say “Subhaana Rabbiya Al-A‘alaa”, as usual.

01:13:09.000 --> 01:13:16.000
So, you only listen to the imam when he recites Al-Fãtehah in the standing position.

01:13:16.000 --> 01:13:23.000
If a person comes late, and finds the Jama’a, the group, already did one or two or three

01:13:23.000 --> 01:13:29.000
Rak’as, units, you just – if you come late, you just join the group in whatever

01:13:29.000 --> 01:13:33.000
position they are in, and then after they finish, when they say “Al-Salaamu ‘Alaykum”,

01:13:33.000 --> 01:13:39.000
the first one, you stand up and you complete the part that you missed.

01:13:39.000 --> 01:13:45.000
So, this is how you make up for missing units, or missing Rak’as when you join a group.

01:14:04.000 --> 01:14:08.000
What happens if you miss one of the prayers, one of the Contact Prayers?

01:14:08.000 --> 01:14:16.000
You're supposed to do all five Contact Prayers during each one of the five periods, the Morning

01:14:16.000 --> 01:14:21.000
Contact before sunrise, the Noon between around 12:00 and four (16:00), the Afternoon

01:14:21.000 --> 01:14:26.000
between four (16:00) and sunset, the Sunset Contact immediately after sunset, and the

01:14:26.000 --> 01:14:34.000
Night Prayer after all the twilight disappears from the horizon, about two hours after sunset.

01:14:34.000 --> 01:14:37.000
Now what happens if you miss one of these prayers?

01:14:37.000 --> 01:14:43.000
There is a myth that you can make it up or combine prayers and it is just an innovation.

01:14:43.000 --> 01:14:46.000
You cannot make up missed prayer.

01:14:46.000 --> 01:14:51.000
If you miss the Noon Prayer in any day, you just cannot bring yesterday back.

01:14:51.000 --> 01:14:53.000
You missed it and it is too bad.

01:14:53.000 --> 01:15:00.000
So, you just ask God for forgiveness, repent and promise God that you will never, to the

01:15:00.000 --> 01:15:05.000
best of your ability, miss anymore prayers, and you just go on doing the prayers.

01:15:05.000 --> 01:15:13.000
See, the idea of the Contact Prayer is to contact our creator within a certain period of every day.

01:15:13.000 --> 01:15:17.000
And when you miss that, it is gone. You cannot bring it back, and you cannot make

01:15:17.000 --> 01:15:23.000
it up, but you can ask forgives and repent.

01:15:23.000 --> 01:15:31.000
And now the best way to describe the Contact Prayers to you is to demonstrate exactly how it is done.

01:15:31.000 --> 01:15:37.000
So, now I will demonstrate for you the Morning Contact Prayer.

01:15:49.000 --> 01:15:55.000
Do you remember the first thing you have to do in order to observe the Contact Prayers?

01:15:55.000 --> 01:16:00.000
That’s right, the intention. You declare your intention, in Arabic “NIYYA.

01:16:00.000 --> 01:16:06.000
So, since this is the morning prayer, I will make the intention for the Morning Contact Prayer,

01:16:06.000 --> 01:16:08.000
in English then in Arabic.

01:16:08.000 --> 01:16:13.000
Then, I will proceed with the prayer and you just watch everything I'm doing and this

01:16:13.000 --> 01:16:18.000
is – this should be the correct way for observing the Contact Prayer.

01:16:18.000 --> 01:16:25.000
